9-541a-ab16-d958e9ccc367" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247123 #edb/ref 1074 "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the first row of ${I}_{3}$ by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{1}:=5{R}_{1}$ to $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247125 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247125 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110471" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247125 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247125 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the elementary row operation \n${R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247125 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "19a88f9a-52c5-5b2c-8ad4-1823f5f13230" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247125 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247127 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247127 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110487" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247127 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247127 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{3}:=-4{R}_{3}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247127 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ef7377c9-957a-58e5-9785-2a3ba9f3dc5b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247127 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:=-4{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-4{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247129 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247129 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110494" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247129 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247129 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247129 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "41dfac52-4d1d-591c-8036-6625f46b98d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247129 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299992 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299992 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299992 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0bc404a6-d316-58c1-b56c-a595600e5fdc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300017 #edb/ref 1080 "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300017 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300017 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0f052266-a78d-53f6-a624-dbcfb60c6b7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300081 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300081 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186300081 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1a9c3794-3d61-5c59-8f4c-0fba7faa0d24" #edb/ref 17